From 30f3a31c963148702ac5fccd60c9599a1e969c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:35:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] util/Globo: the bar's own tooltips, hanging from the
 bar edge; menus too

GTK 4 places a tooltip window 4 px below the widget (gtk_tooltip_position pads the
anchor rect by 4 px) and offers no way to move it, so a bar that wants tooltips fused
to its bottom edge, in the style of its menus and panels, cannot use them.

util::Globo replaces them: a Gtk::Popover without arrow, focus or input (can-target
false), parented to the module widget, positioned BOTTOM with a y offset equal to the
distance from the widget's bottom to the window's bottom, so it starts exactly at the
bar's edge. It keeps GTK's timings (500 ms, 60 ms in browse mode), hides on leave and
on click, and updates live while open (volume while scrolling). It has the CSS class
"globo" plus the bar window's classes (output name, bar name, position) so style.css
can style each bar differently; the same classes are added to the "menu-file" popover
menus, which now get the same y offset.

AModule creates it in bindEvents() for the bound widget and re-anchors it when the
widget changes (ALabel binds the label first, AIconLabel rebinds the box; the label is
0 px wide for icon-only modules). Modules keep setting tooltips as before: ALabel
serves its stored markup through globoMarkup(), other modules through the widget's
tooltip property, whose has-tooltip flag the globo keeps off so GTK never shows its own.
Tray items (sni::Item) get one too.

